#: includes/addons_help.php:30
msgid "What this screen lists."
msgstr ""

#: includes/addons_help.php:31
msgid "Two things at once: the add-ons installed on this site, and the ones published at the store that are not installed yet."
msgstr ""

#: includes/addons_help.php:32
msgid "An installed add-on shows its version and the actions it accepts; one that is only at the store shows what it costs or which membership includes it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/addons_help.php:33
msgid "WPeMatico add-ons are hidden from the main Plugins list by default. Settings &rsaquo; Writing &rsaquo; \"See local Addons in plugin list\" puts them back among the other plugins; this screen works the same either way."
msgstr ""

#: includes/addons_help.php:36
msgid "The views, the counter and the search box."
msgstr ""

#: includes/addons_help.php:37
msgid "Active, Inactive and the rest count only what is installed, so the store catalogue appears under All and in search results only."
msgstr ""

#: includes/addons_help.php:38
msgid "The number beside \"WPeMatico Addons\" in the menu is how many installed add-ons have an update waiting."
msgstr ""

#: includes/addons_help.php:39
msgid "Typing in the search box hides the rows on screen as you type; pressing Enter searches the whole list, catalogue included."
msgstr ""

#: includes/addons_help.php:42
msgid "The button on each row."
msgstr ""

#: includes/addons_help.php:43
msgid "Activate starts an add-on that is installed and stopped. Enable auto-updates appears once it is running and its license is valid."
msgstr ""

#: includes/addons_help.php:44
msgid "Add license, Renew license, Activate license and Check license each point at one precise thing: hover the button and it says which."
msgstr ""

#: includes/addons_help.php:45
msgid "Installed, with no other action, means the switch cannot be offered here: either this site runs no automatic updates at all, or your user cannot update plugins."
msgstr ""

#: includes/addons_help.php:48 includes/campaigns_list_help.php:91
msgid "Bulk actions."
msgstr ""

#: includes/addons_help.php:49
msgid "Select rows and apply Activate, Deactivate, Delete or the auto-update actions. They are WordPress' own actions, applied exactly as they are on the Plugins screen."
msgstr ""

#: includes/addons_help.php:50
msgid "An add-on can only be deleted while it is deactivated, and WPeMatico itself cannot be deactivated while an add-on depends on it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/addons_help.php:53
msgid "Automatic updates"
msgstr ""

#: includes/addons_help.php:55
msgid "What to expect when you turn them on."
msgstr ""

#: includes/addons_help.php:56
msgid "Nothing happens at that moment. WordPress checks for updates about twice a day and installs them on its own schedule, so a new version can land several hours after it is published."
msgstr ""

#: includes/addons_help.php:57
msgid "Automatic updates are run by WP-Cron. On a site where cron does not fire, they never run — Tools &rsaquo; System Status reports that."
msgstr ""

#: includes/addons_help.php:58
msgid "WordPress emails the site administrator after it installs an update, and when one fails."
msgstr ""

#: includes/addons_help.php:61
msgid "WPeMatico updates first, always."
msgstr ""

#: includes/addons_help.php:62
msgid "An add-on extends the core plugin, so it is never installed ahead of it. While WPeMatico has an update pending, add-on updates wait — by hand and automatically alike."
msgstr ""

#: includes/addons_help.php:63
msgid "That is why turning automatic updates on for an add-on turns them on for WPeMatico as well: with both on, the add-on installs right after the core plugin, unattended."
msgstr ""

#: includes/addons_help.php:64
msgid "You can turn WPeMatico's back off, and nothing stops you — but then its add-ons stay on the version they have until you update WPeMatico by hand. This screen says so when that is the case."
msgstr ""

#: includes/addons_help.php:67
msgid "An add-on that is waiting says so."
msgstr ""

#: includes/addons_help.php:68
msgid "When an unattended update is held back, the row says what it is waiting for and since when, instead of failing quietly."
msgstr ""

#: includes/addons_help.php:69
msgid "Updating WPeMatico clears it: the next check installs the add-on with no further action."
msgstr ""

#: includes/addons_help.php:72
msgid "Sites where they cannot run."
msgstr ""

#: includes/addons_help.php:73
msgid "Some hosts manage updates themselves, and a site under version control, or one with automatic updates disabled by a constant, does not run them either."
msgstr ""

#: includes/addons_help.php:74
msgid "The toggle is not offered there. The row says the add-on keeps its version until it is updated by hand."
msgstr ""

