#: includes/feed_list_help.php:31
msgid "What the Feed List shows."
msgstr ""

#: includes/feed_list_help.php:32
msgid "Every feed URL configured on this site, one row per feed, no matter which campaign holds it. A campaign with five feeds appears in five rows."
msgstr ""

#: includes/feed_list_help.php:33
msgid "It answers the questions the campaign list cannot: whether a URL is already being imported, which campaign owns it, and whether the same feed was added twice."
msgstr ""

#: includes/feed_list_help.php:34
msgid "This is a read-only view. Everything is edited from the campaign itself."
msgstr ""

#: includes/feed_list_help.php:38
msgid "The address exactly as the campaign stores it, which is what gets requested on every run."
msgstr ""

#: includes/feed_list_help.php:39
msgid "Seeing the same address in two rows means two campaigns import it; that is legitimate when they publish differently, and a duplicate-post source when they do not."
msgstr ""

#: includes/feed_list_help.php:42
msgid "Campaign."
msgstr ""

#: includes/feed_list_help.php:43
msgid "The campaign this feed belongs to. The name links to its edit screen, where the feed can be changed or removed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/feed_list_help.php:46
msgid "Status."
msgstr ""

#: includes/feed_list_help.php:47
msgid "Whether the campaign is active, that is, whether the scheduler runs it. Feeds are not activated one by one: the state belongs to the campaign, so every row of the same campaign shows the same value."
msgstr ""

#: includes/feed_list_help.php:48
msgid "An inactive campaign is never fetched automatically, but can still be run by hand from the campaign list."
msgstr ""

#: includes/feed_list_help.php:51
msgid "Last run."
msgstr ""

#: includes/feed_list_help.php:52
msgid "When the campaign last completed a run — again a campaign-wide value, not a per-feed one. \"Never\" means it has not run since it was created or since its log was cleared."
msgstr ""

#: includes/feed_list_help.php:53
msgid "A campaign that is active but has not run in a long time usually means cron is not firing. The Tools &rsaquo; System tab checks that."
msgstr ""

#: includes/feed_list_help.php:56
msgid "Actions."
msgstr ""

#: includes/feed_list_help.php:57
msgid "Edit campaign opens the campaign that holds this feed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/feed_list_help.php:58
msgid "Inspect in Feed Viewer requests the URL and shows the raw answer, which is the fastest way to tell a broken feed from a broken campaign."
msgstr ""

#: includes/feed_list_help.php:59
msgid "Open URL loads the address in a new browser tab, as your browser sees it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/feed_list_help.php:62
msgid "Searching and filtering."
msgstr ""

#: includes/feed_list_help.php:63
msgid "The box works at two scopes. As you type it hides, right away, the rows of the page you are looking at — useful to spot one feed among the ones already on screen."
msgstr ""

#: includes/feed_list_help.php:64
msgid "Pressing Enter or the button searches every feed of the site instead, across all pages, and the list is rebuilt with the matches: the counter, the pages and the sorting all apply to the result."
msgstr ""

#: includes/feed_list_help.php:65
msgid "It matches the feed URL and the campaign name. Esc clears the instant filter, and \"Clear search\" undoes the global one."
msgstr ""

#: includes/feed_list_help.php:68
msgid "Sorting and page size."
msgstr ""

#: includes/feed_list_help.php:69
msgid "Click any underlined column header to sort by it, and again to reverse the order. Sorting applies to the whole list, not only to the page on screen."
msgstr ""

#: includes/feed_list_help.php:70
msgid "How many rows each page shows is set under Screen Options, at the top right of this screen."
msgstr ""

#: includes/feed_viewer_help.php:32
msgid "What the Feed Viewer is for."
msgstr ""

#: includes/feed_viewer_help.php:33
msgid "It asks a URL for its content exactly the way a campaign does, and shows you the raw answer without creating any post."
msgstr ""

#: includes/feed_viewer_help.php:34
msgid "Use it before adding a feed to a campaign, or when a campaign fetches nothing and you need to know whether the problem is the source, the network or the campaign settings."
msgstr ""

#: includes/feed_viewer_help.php:35
msgid "Nothing is saved, published or cached: it only reads the URL and prints what came back."
msgstr ""

#: includes/feed_viewer_help.php:39
msgid "Paste the address of the feed itself (it usually ends in /feed/, /rss, .xml or similar), not the address of the site that publishes it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/feed_viewer_help.php:40
msgid "Only http:// and https:// addresses are accepted. If the feed needs a key or a token, include it in the URL just as the campaign would use it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/feed_viewer_help.php:41
msgid "Arriving from the eye icon of a campaign feed, or from the Feed List, fills this field in and fetches it right away."
msgstr ""

#: includes/feed_viewer_help.php:44
msgid "Get Feed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/feed_viewer_help.php:45
msgid "Requests the URL with the same parser, user agent and timeouts the campaigns use, so what you see here is what a campaign would receive."
msgstr ""

#: includes/feed_viewer_help.php:46
msgid "The result is a coloured message with the summary and the headers, and the complete unmodified answer in the box below."
msgstr ""

#: includes/feed_viewer_help.php:49
msgid "Green result: the feed was parsed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/feed_viewer_help.php:50
msgid "The URL is a valid RSS or Atom feed. The summary names its format, its title and how many items it carries, and the box shows the XML as the source sent it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/feed_viewer_help.php:51
msgid "Zero items means the feed is valid but empty right now: a campaign on it would fetch nothing until the source publishes again."
msgstr ""

#: includes/feed_viewer_help.php:52
msgid "A line reading \"Feed found by autodiscovery\" means you pasted a page, not a feed, and the site advertised one: that is the address to use, because a site may stop advertising it at any time."
msgstr ""

#: includes/feed_viewer_help.php:53
msgid "This is the answer before any campaign filter runs, so anything missing here will also be missing in the campaign."
msgstr ""

#: includes/feed_viewer_help.php:56
msgid "Yellow result: it answers, but it is not a feed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/feed_viewer_help.php:57
msgid "The parser rejected the content, so the URL was requested again as a plain page to show you what is really there. The reason given by the parser is printed first."
msgstr ""

#: includes/feed_viewer_help.php:58
msgid "An HTTP code of 200 with HTML in the box means you pasted the address of a page instead of its feed. Codes 401 or 403 mean the source is refusing the request, and 404 that the address no longer exists."
msgstr ""

#: includes/feed_viewer_help.php:59
msgid "Many sites answer 200 with a \"please enable JavaScript\" or an anti-bot page; that content in the box is the source blocking automated readers, not a plugin failure."
msgstr ""

#: includes/feed_viewer_help.php:62
msgid "Red result: the URL could not be reached."
msgstr ""

#: includes/feed_viewer_help.php:63
msgid "The request never got an answer, so the box shows the network error instead of content. It is a problem between your server and the source, not a problem with the feed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/feed_viewer_help.php:64
msgid "Typical causes are a name that does not resolve, an expired or invalid SSL certificate, a firewall on your hosting blocking outgoing requests, or a source too slow to answer before the timeout."
msgstr ""

#: includes/feed_viewer_help.php:65
msgid "If several unrelated feeds fail the same way, check the outgoing request tests on the Tools &rsaquo; System tab before blaming the sources."
msgstr ""

#: includes/feed_viewer_help.php:68
msgid "Response headers."
msgstr ""

#: includes/feed_viewer_help.php:69
msgid "What the source replied about its own answer. The interesting ones are content-type (a feed should be xml, not html), last-modified and etag, which tell you how fresh the content is."
msgstr ""

#: includes/feed_viewer_help.php:70
msgid "A content-type of text/html on a URL that still parses is usually a badly configured server, and is worth knowing when the source starts failing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/feed_viewer_help.php:73
msgid "Raw content box."
msgstr ""

#: includes/feed_viewer_help.php:74
msgid "The complete answer, untouched. Read it to confirm a feed really carries the tags you expect — full content, images, categories, custom fields — before setting a campaign to use them."
msgstr ""

#: includes/feed_viewer_help.php:75
msgid "Use Copy to put it on the clipboard; it is what our support team asks for when a feed behaves strangely."
msgstr ""

